          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tīkṣṇa is built on the root √tij, \"to be or become sharp\" (MW). In the Rigveda it means \"sharp\", later also \"hot, pungent\" (CDIAL 5839). It lives on as Hindi tīkhā, \"sharp, pungent\". MW compares √tij with Greek stizō, \"I prick\"."
            }
