          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mūlyavān is the nominative of mūlyavat, built on mūlya, \"original value, price\", and the suffix -vat, \"having\" (MW). Mūlya comes from mūla, \"root\", so a price is the root value of a thing (CDIAL 10257). Gujarati mūl, \"price\", comes from it."
            }
